      "content": "When a dedicated athlete causes an injury like a runner's knee, the identity that once thrived around the sport often suffers, leaving behind a quiet space where the person you were serves no one. This period can feel empty precisely because your life did reach a meaningful peak; the crash creates a depth of experience that rushing past a new beginning would miss. Give yourself permission to simply exist without the expectation of finding growth or purpose immediately, for you can still find dignity in acknowledging your history and tending to the person left behind.",
